From Digitization and Images to Text and Content:
Transkribus as a Case Study
Gila Prebor Bar-Ilan University
Over the past decades, libraries and archives have been increasingly investing in the digitization of their collections, including manuscripts, rare books, newspapers, and archival material. Many of these resources are freely accessible. However, the accessible material consists only of the metadata of the resources along with their images. The textual content of the resulting digital images is not yet visible, and those seeking to find the content of the resources must study and transcribe individual passages.
