The purpose of this article is to discuss the potential inherent in the use of technological tools in the transcription of Hebrew manuscripts. The paper is structured as follows: First, I give a brief overview of automatic text recognition in general and in Hebrew letters specifically. This is followed by a review of the Transkribus platform and the models that I used and trained using the Transkribus platform with a Sephardic semicursive fifteenth-­century script. I then analyze their performance, comparing a generic model to a specific model. I conclude with a discussion of the implications of Transkribus’s capabilities for automatic transcription of historical handwritten Hebrew manuscripts.4
Automatic Text Recognition (ATR)
The digitization of historical resources is accomplished by professionally photographing and scanning the various resources. This digitization makes historical documents accessible and contributes to the preservation of
